# Version format — `yy.m.ddbb`

Use this format for **all releases** in this repo and when bootstrapping **new projects** from this template.

## Structure (semver 3-part)

| Segment | Meaning | Range |
|---------|---------|-------|
| `yy` | 2-digit year | 0–99 |
| `m` | month | 1–12 |
| `ddbb` | patch = `day * 100 + build` | day 1–31, build 1–99 |

**Example:** `26.6.1101` = 2026-06-11, build 1  
**Release tag:** `v.26.6.1101` (unsigned: `v.26.6.1101-unsigned`)

## Decode patch (`ddbb`)

```
day   = floor(patch / 100)
build = patch % 100
```

## Why not `yy.mdd.build`?

`mdd` in the minor segment (e.g. `611`) exceeds **Windows MSI minor ≤ 255**.  
`yy.m.ddbb` keeps minor ≤ 12 and works with Tauri/Cargo/MSI without overrides.

## Files to keep in sync

- `VERSION`
- `package.json` / `package-lock.json`
- `src/version.ts` (`APP_VERSION`)
- `src-tauri/Cargo.toml` / `Cargo.lock`
- `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`
- `src-tauri/tauri.windows.conf.json` (WiX, when present)
- `design-pack/version.ts` (if design-pack is used)

## Bump rules

- Same calendar day, new release → increment **build** only: `26.6.1101` → `26.6.1102`
- New day → reset build to 1: `26.6.1201` (Jun 12, build 1)

## Validation

```bash
npm run validate:version
```

